1.2. The right of use includes installing the Software on one or more servers under the Licensee's control, running it,
     configuring it through the means provided by its interface and command line, and making the backup copies
     strictly necessary for its preservation.
1.3. The Software remains the property of the Licensor at all times. Nothing in this licence transfers any
     intellectual property right to the Licensee.

2. EDITIONS

2.1. Personal edition. The Personal edition is granted free of charge for personal, non-commercial use, limited to five
     (5) websites per installation. No licence key is required. Personal use excludes, in particular, hosting third
     parties for a fee, reselling hosting, and any commercial hosting or managed-services activity.
2.2. Professional and Enterprise editions. The features of the Professional and Enterprise editions are subject to a
     valid licence key and to the terms of sale published at https://toutpanel.com (term, number of servers, number of
     websites, support, updates). The licence key is personal to the Licensee and bound to the server on which it is
     activated.
2.3. Using a feature reserved for a paid edition without a valid key, or beyond the limits of the key, is a breach of
     this licence.

3. RESTRICTIONS

